 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Structure",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Two avalanche TVS diodes share one anode on pin 3; their cathodes are pins 1 and 2. From pin 1 to pin 2 the two diodes are in series, anode to anode, and that path protects one bidirectional line."
  },
  {
   "topic": "One-line wiring",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "For a single line at under 1 pF, the line goes to pin 1 or pin 2 and the other of the two goes to ground; pin 3 is left open. In this wiring the part serves lines running above 3 GHz. The ground side goes straight into a ground plane by the shortest path, to keep parasitic inductance down."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Two-line wiring",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "For two lines, one line goes to pin 1 and the other to pin 2, with pin 3 to ground. In this wiring the part serves lines running above 2.0 GHz. Pin 3 goes straight into a ground plane by the shortest path, to keep parasitic inductance down."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Listed uses: MDDI, USB 2.0 and USB 3.0, HDMI, Infiniband transceivers, antenna circuits, automatic test equipment, GaAs photodetectors and HBT power amplifiers. Rated for no insertion loss up to beyond 3.0 GHz."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction and assembly",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "Solid-state silicon-avalanche diodes in an SC-75 (SOT-523) body moulded in UL 94V-0 compound, under 1 mm high. Leads are 100 % matte tin with no other alloy added; the part is lead-free, halogen-free and RoHS/WEEE compliant. The lead finish carries little solder against the paste printed on the land pattern, so reflow follows the paste's profile; lead-free and SnPb assembly both apply."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "The top carries P5 and a two-character date code YW."
  }
 ],
